// Scene Size: 200
// Scene Grid: 20

// A 120 mm tile of dried mud. Cellular noise lays out the plates (sampled
// in 3D; 14 mm cells against 3 mm of relief keep the walls near vertical).
// Along each cell wall the surface drops into a 3 mm crack, and just before
// the drop the plate edges curl up, the way drying clay shrinks and lifts.
// Both are real geometry. The plates are the measured clay colour, paler
// where they have dried at the top of each curl and darker down in the
// cracks.

clayMat, clayColor = physical.clay();

walls = noise.cellularEdges(14);
curl = 0.6 * clamp(1 - walls / 5, 0, 1);
crack = 3 * max(0, 1 - walls / 0.8);
top = curl - crack;

block = boxCentered([0, 0, -5], [120, 120, 10]);
mud = intersectSharp(block, p.z - top);

dry = color.lighten(clayColor, 0.15);
damp = color.darken(clayColor, 0.45);
plate = color.mixOklab(clayColor, dry, texture.mask(p.z + 0.2 * noise.gradient(6), 0.2, 0.3));
mud.material = clayMat;
mud.color = texture.paint(walls, 0.8, 0.5, damp, plate);

return mud;
